# Database

PostgreSQL is the source of schedule and job state. Alembic is the only schema path. Add a new revision under `backend/alembic/versions` and keep `models.py` aligned. Do not edit an already applied revision.

Use timezone-aware `DateTime(timezone=True)`. Store campaign timezone separately as an IANA id.

Partial unique indexes protect one schedule post per campaign slot and one active Threads user id. Use `sql_text` for `postgresql_where`: the `Post.text` column must not shadow SQLAlchemy `text()`.

Job claims rely on `FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`. Integration tests that cover claiming or recovery must use Testcontainers PostgreSQL, not SQLite.

Do not store plaintext tokens. The token column holds Fernet ciphertext.
